// control.v1: the devbox control plane (what's needed now).
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// DEFINITION (INFRA == CONTROL)
//   Control owns everything it runs that ISN'T a tether binary and doesn't
//   talk to one: operations on the "physical" layer, i.e. the VM, docker,
//   ssh forwards, and starting and running pairs.
//   Anything that only talks to a separate running app is a PAIR, not control
//   (clip, notify, open, approve, xcb, snap, feedback...).
//
//   It runs as the tether pair `control`: the VM gateway is on
//   DEVBOX_CONTROL_PORT (published on VM loopback), the Mac gateway is
//   dialled through an ssh unix-socket forward, and the token is
//   DISPATCH_TOKEN.
//   Mac side = `dev`. VM side = controld.
//
// RULES
//   1. The Mac is in charge. Mac → VM calls declare desired state;
//      VM → Mac calls are requests that `dev` carries out.
//   2. One user, full access. Being authenticated from Sam's machines is the
//      security boundary. No roles, no policy engine.
//   3. Who's asking travels with requests. tether-gw stamps the caller's
//      SO_PEERCRED (uid, pid) on every call. For control, controld
//      also puts the ORIGINAL requester (e.g. the `bb forward` process)
//      into the request, so forwards are labelled and attributed per instance.
//   4. Pairs and forwards are session-scoped: released when the session ends
//      or after 30s without the control connection. Services are not: they
//      keep running after the session ends.
//   5. control.v1 changes in place; there is one user and no compatibility
//      to keep.
//
// VERSIONS
//   A schema change changes the hash, and the gateway refuses a mismatch.
//   `dev` and the image carry the same devbox.lock, so both sides run the
//   control version it names.
//
// ERRORS (Connect codes)
//   invalid_argument     bad shape or values (port < 1024, reserved port, bad host)
//   failed_precondition  the Mac port is in use by something else, or a static
//                        forward can't be removed from the VM
//   resource_exhausted   more than DEVBOX_MAX_FORWARDS dynamic forwards this session
//   unavailable          the peer is down (fails fast)
//
// RESERVED PORTS (never exposed or auto-forwarded)
//   DEVBOX_RESERVED_PORTS, and any static forward from config
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

